{
  "name": "barbel",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/fish/barbel.py): a common barbel, 60 cm -- LONG and low with a FLAT BELLY and a gently arched back, a long pointed snout over an UNDERSLUNG mouth with thick fleshy lips and FOUR BARBELS (`horn`s: a short pair at the snout, a longer pair at the mouth's corners); a short high dorsal with a stiff serrated first ray, pelvics under it, a small anal, low pectorals, a forked tail; bronze-olive above, golden flanks over rowed scales, a pale belly, the pectorals, pelvics, anal and the tail's LOWER lobe orange-red. Each fin is one membrane sheet. A SWIMMER (the fish's plumbing; it keeps low, near the bottom).",
